# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cartoona — Docker runtime environment (TEMPLATE, V0.1.35)
#
#   cp .env.docker.example .env.docker     then fill in real values locally.
#
# PLACEHOLDERS ONLY in this file. `.env.docker` is gitignored and must never be
# committed, and nothing from it is ever copied into the image — compose passes
# it to the container at run time (`env_file`).
#
# Two groups of variables:
#   1. CURRENT — Supabase. The app's database, auth and storage. Required.
#   2. LOCAL POSTGRESQL (V0.1.37) — the local `postgres` service. Prepared but
#      NOT WIRED: the app does not read these yet.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ══ 1. CURRENT — Supabase and app runtime ═════════════════════════════════════

# ── BUILD-TIME *and* RUNTIME ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are inlined into the browser bundle by `next build`, so
# the browser gets whatever was present at build time, while server code reads
# them from the container environment at run time. Supply them BOTH ways, with
# the same values — see docs/DOCKER.md ("Environment variables").
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# ── RUNTIME ONLY — never a build arg, never in an image layer ────────────────
# Supabase secret (service-role) key. Server-side only.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=your-secret-key-here
# Project ref of the project above (the part before .supabase.co).
SUPABASE_PROJECT_REF=your-project-ref

# ── RUNTIME ONLY — rate limiting (V0.1.32) ───────────────────────────────────
# Secret used to hash client identifiers in rate-limit keys. Set any long
# random string; leave empty to accept the built-in default behaviour.
RATE_LIMIT_HASH_SECRET=
# Header to trust for the client IP. Only set this when a proxy you control
# sets it — behind nothing, leave it empty so the socket address is used.
RATE_LIMIT_TRUSTED_IP_HEADER=
# "true" disables enforcement. Leave empty for a prod-like container.
RATE_LIMIT_DISABLED=

# ── RUNTIME ONLY — logging ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# debug | info | warn | error. Defaults to info.
LOG_LEVEL=

# ══ 2. LOCAL POSTGRESQL (V0.1.37) — prepared, NOT used by the app yet ════════
# Read by compose for the `postgres` service, so export this file (or pass
# `--env-file .env.docker`) when running compose — see docs/DOCKER.md.
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD has no default: left empty, the database refuses to start
# (the web app is unaffected). Use a URL-safe value, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 24`,
# so it can be pasted into the URLs below unescaped.
POSTGRES_DB=cartoona
POSTGRES_USER=cartoona
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=your-postgres-password
# For a backend inside the compose network (V0.1.38+): service name, port 5432.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://cartoona:your-postgres-password@postgres:5432/cartoona
# For tools on this Mac (psql, migrations): loopback, published port 5433.
LOCAL_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://cartoona:your-postgres-password@localhost:5433/cartoona

# ── Backend (V0.1.40) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The backend connects as a RESTRICTED login role (member of cartoona_app),
# never as the owner above. Create it once, after migrations, with:
#   CARTOONA_APP_DB_PASSWORD=... DATABASE_URL="$LOCAL_DATABASE_URL" scripts/db/app-login-role.sh
# Generate the password with: openssl rand -hex 32
CARTOONA_APP_DB_PASSWORD=your-app-db-password
BACKEND_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://cartoona_app_login:your-app-db-password@postgres:5432/cartoona

# ── Backend address for the frontend (V0.1.41) ───────────────────────────────
# Not set here: compose gives the frontend BACKEND_INTERNAL_URL=http://backend:4000
# itself. Optional override of the single-attempt timeout (250-15000, default 3000):
# BACKEND_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=3000
# NOTE: this whole file is handed to the frontend container, but compose blanks
# every database variable above (POSTGRES_*, DATABASE_URL, LOCAL_DATABASE_URL,
# CARTOONA_APP_DB_PASSWORD, BACKEND_DATABASE_URL) for it. Keep database secrets
# in the database sections only.

# ── Deliberately NOT set in a prod-like container ────────────────────────────
# These are development-only switches. The server also refuses them when
# NODE_ENV=production, which it is in this image. Keep them unset.
# CARTOONA_ENABLE_DEV_PAYMENT_SIMULATION=
# DEV_PARENT_AUTH_ENABLED=
# DEV_PARENT_AUTH_SECRET=
#
# Destructive/stateful test variables (CARTOONA_TEST_*,
# CARTOONA_ALLOW_DESTRUCTIVE_TESTS) belong in .env.local for local test runs
# ONLY. Never pass them to a container.
